From: Ghaf contributors
Subject: [PATCH] crosvm: Accept upstream protected KVM creation

Upstream arm64 KVM reports protected-VM support by accepting
KVM_CREATE_VM with KVM_VM_TYPE_ARM_PROTECTED. It does not expose the
Android-only KVM_CAP_ARM_PROTECTED_VM capability number that Crosvm probes
after creating the VM.

Treat successful creation as authoritative for the KVM backend. Kernels
without upstream pKVM protected-guest support reject the protected VM type
during KvmVm::new().

---
 src/crosvm/sys/linux.rs | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/crosvm/sys/linux.rs b/src/crosvm/sys/linux.rs
index d7eb6a4..886721d 100644
--- a/src/crosvm/sys/linux.rs
+++ b/src/crosvm/sys/linux.rs
@@ -162,6 +162,10 @@ use hypervisor::HypervisorCap;
 use hypervisor::MemCacheType;
 use hypervisor::ProtectionType;
 use hypervisor::Vm;
+#[cfg(all(
+    target_arch = "aarch64",
+    any(feature = "geniezone", feature = "gunyah", feature = "halla")
+))]
 use hypervisor::VmCap;
 use jail::*;
 #[cfg(feature = "pci-hotplug")]
@@ -2138,7 +2138,4 @@ fn run_kvm(device_path: Option<&Path>, cfg: Config, components: VmComponents) ->
-    // Check that the VM was actually created in protected mode as expected.
-    // This check is only needed on aarch64. On x86_64, protected VM creation will fail
-    // if protected mode is not supported.
-    #[cfg(not(target_arch = "x86_64"))]
-    if cfg.protection_type.isolates_memory() && !vm.check_capability(VmCap::Protected) {
-        bail!("Failed to create protected VM");
-    }
+    // Upstream arm64 KVM rejects KVM_CREATE_VM with the protected type when
+    // protected mode is unavailable. Reaching this point therefore confirms
+    // that KvmVm::new() created the requested protected VM. The legacy
+    // KVM_CAP_ARM_PROTECTED_VM probe is specific to Android's downstream ABI.
